# ---- the game's own modes (item 164): its mode TABLE, walked by the runtime (MODE_SDK.md "The game's own
# modes"): the array the get-mode-by-id accessor reads, the cmode class's ACTIVE slot (Godzilla's 14, found
# by its body), START (active - 6), the typeinfos that tell a cmode and a multiball (cmode_mball) apart
data stock_mode_table       0x0b5b66b0
value stock_mode_count      36
value stock_slot_active     46
value stock_slot_start      40
data typeinfo_cmode         0x00507e44
data typeinfo_cmode_mball   0x005092dc
data typeinfo_vmi           0x00502094

# ---- a mode's own screen (item 164): the scene lookup's typed finders (find_node casts to Radium::Sprite,
# find_text to Radium::Text; found through the lookup, Godzilla LE 1.16 0x587bac, by the class each casts to),
# the node's set-visible (Sprite slot 42) and the scene inside a scene player
site find_node        0x0046d1bc 0xe92d4070 0xe24dd008
site find_text        0x0046cc58 0xe92d4070 0xe24dd008
# Insider Connected score gate (item 166): the request header constructor (the endpoint in r1) and the
# message-begin thunk every sender calls next; the runtime refuses the score reports there
# (MODE_SDK.md, "Insider Connected: no score leaves a machine that carries modes")
site agent_header     0x004b9c50 0xe92d40f8 0xe2505000
site agent_begin      0x004c45ac 0xe590c004 0xe1a00001
value node_visible_vfn      0xa8
value scene_player_scene    0x10

# ---- a mode's own screen goes in this scene: drawn every frame of a game (item 164, the RadiumScene census)
scene hud                  28aff8e66e7c61dc4722a30ee31e22d1afe094d6/efd9321ee61c0467eaaecb1369842d69eed4a6aa
